01:05:16.621 --> 01:05:18.122
Oh, no.

01:05:18.539 --> 01:05:20.499
No, no.

01:05:21.584 --> 01:05:25.796
I know my behavior can be 
erratic sometimes.

01:05:27.006 --> 01:05:28.382
What do you want me to do?

01:05:29.008 --> 01:05:30.176
What is it that you want?

01:05:30.259 --> 01:05:33.596
If you really want to do something for me, 
then stop making this scene right now.

01:05:33.679 --> 01:05:36.849
- Oh, God, I can't believe this. 
-l'm leaving.

01:05:36.932 --> 01:05:39.226
I've assessed the situation, 
and I'm going.

01:05:39.852 --> 01:05:40.937
Where are you going?

01:05:41.020 --> 01:05:42.647
Just leaving.

01:05:42.897 --> 01:05:43.856
But where?

01:05:45.483 --> 01:05:47.526
I have to return some videotapes.

01:06:15.307 --> 01:06:18.807
[Edit: “Feed me a stray cat” ATM beat and the witness murder (Remaster cues “Here, kitty, kitty.” / “Oh, my God]

01:06:18.957 --> 01:06:23.993
that stretch is widely read as in his head (an ATM cannot say that), so cutting it leaves a dream-like chase that starts for unclear reasons.

01:06:24.143 --> 01:06:27.928
Unspoken: he already knows he’s guilty of various murders — a just-now kill is not what he’s running from.

01:06:28.078 --> 01:06:32.186
Homeless Al murder out (~00:20–00:22) — after business-card sweat; resumes at the spa skin beat (“beautiful skin”).

01:06:51.465 --> 01:06:53.467
Drop the weapon! Drop it now!

01:06:53.884 --> 01:06:55.386
Get on the ground! Put--

01:07:39.013 --> 01:07:40.890
Burning the midnight oil, Mr. Smith?

01:07:41.223 --> 01:07:43.100
Hey, now don't forget to sign in.

01:09:13.232 --> 01:09:15.901
Harold, it's Bateman, Patrick Bateman.

01:09:16.902 --> 01:09:18.404
You're my lawyer, 
so I think you should know

01:09:18.487 --> 01:09:19.697
I've killed a lot of people.

01:09:19.780 --> 01:09:22.741
Some escort girls in the apartment uptown,

01:09:23.826 --> 01:09:26.245
some homeless people, maybe five or ten,

01:09:26.328 --> 01:09:28.122
an NYU girl I met in Central Park.

01:09:28.205 --> 01:09:30.374
I left her in a parking lot 
behind some doughnut shop.

01:09:30.457 --> 01:09:33.002
I killed Bethany, 
my old girlfriend, with a nail gun,

01:09:33.085 --> 01:09:35.504
and some man,

01:09:35.588 --> 01:09:37.423
some faggot with a dog.

01:09:38.257 --> 01:09:41.302
Last week, I killed another girl

01:09:42.261 --> 01:09:43.679
with a chain saw.

01:09:46.640 --> 01:09:47.766
I had to.

01:09:47.850 --> 01:09:49.685
She almost got away,

01:09:49.768 --> 01:09:51.604
and...

01:09:51.687 --> 01:09:54.106
Someone else there. I can't remember.

01:09:54.189 --> 01:09:55.441
Maybe a model.

01:09:55.983 --> 01:09:57.234
She's dead, too,

01:09:57.610 --> 01:09:59.445
and Paul Allen.

01:09:59.987 --> 01:10:03.449
I killed Paul Allen 
with an ax in the face.

01:10:03.699 --> 01:10:07.077
His body is dissolving 
in a bathtub in Hell's Kitchen.

01:10:08.287 --> 01:10:10.039
I don't want to leave anything out here.

01:10:10.122 --> 01:10:12.625
I guess I've killed maybe 20 people,

01:10:12.917 --> 01:10:14.460
maybe 40.

01:10:16.670 --> 01:10:18.756
I have tapes of a lot of it.

01:10:19.757 --> 01:10:21.675
Some of the girls have seen the tapes.

01:10:22.218 --> 01:10:23.677
I even...

01:10:31.894 --> 01:10:33.562
I ate some of their brains...

01:10:35.898 --> 01:10:37.316
and I tried to cook a little.

01:10:40.778 --> 01:10:42.446
Tonight I...

01:10:43.822 --> 01:10:47.493
I just had to kill a lot of people,

01:10:48.077 --> 01:10:49.620
and...

01:10:53.332 --> 01:10:54.541
I'm not sure

01:10:55.501 --> 01:10:58.504
I'm gonna get away with it this time.

01:11:01.340 --> 01:11:02.841
So, I mean...

01:11:06.095 --> 01:11:07.429
I guess...

01:11:08.055 --> 01:11:09.598
I'm a pretty...

01:11:11.517 --> 01:11:13.727
I mean, I guess I'm a pretty sick guy.

01:11:16.105 --> 01:11:17.481
So...

01:11:18.816 --> 01:11:20.276
if you get back tomorrow,

01:11:22.069 --> 01:11:23.821
I may show up at Harry's Bar.

01:11:24.238 --> 01:11:25.572
So, you know.

01:11:27.324 --> 01:11:29.285
Keep your eyes open.

01:13:48.966 --> 01:13:50.676
Are you my 2:00?

01:13:51.552 --> 01:13:52.761
No.

01:13:54.429 --> 01:13:55.431
Can I help you?

01:13:56.640 --> 01:13:58.225
I'm looking for...

01:13:59.226 --> 01:14:00.936
Paul Allen's place.

01:14:01.687 --> 01:14:03.647
Doesn't he live here?

01:14:03.897 --> 01:14:05.274
No, he doesn't.

01:14:06.108 --> 01:14:07.401
You sure?

01:14:08.819 --> 01:14:10.696
You saw the ad in the Times?

01:14:10.779 --> 01:14:11.989
No.

01:14:12.322 --> 01:14:14.074
Yeah. I mean, yeah.

01:14:14.825 --> 01:14:16.076
In <i>the Times.</i>

01:14:16.160 --> 01:14:17.703
There was no ad in the Times.

01:14:19.037 --> 01:14:20.664
I think you should go now.

01:14:21.331 --> 01:14:22.624
But I think...

01:14:25.586 --> 01:14:27.004
I want to know what happened here.

01:14:27.087 --> 01:14:29.548
Don't make any trouble, please.

01:14:30.424 --> 01:14:31.967
I suggest you 90-

01:14:45.189 --> 01:14:46.482
Don't come back.

01:14:46.773 --> 01:14:47.983
I won't.

01:14:48.817 --> 01:14:50.110
Don't worry.

01:15:21.099 --> 01:15:22.267
Patrick Bateman's office.

01:15:22.351 --> 01:15:23.644
<i>Jean?</i>

01:15:23.727 --> 01:15:25.896
-/ <i>need help.</i> 
- Patrick, is that you?

01:15:27.022 --> 01:15:28.273
Jean, I'm not--

01:15:29.525 --> 01:15:30.901
Craig McDermott called.

01:15:30.984 --> 01:15:34.112
Wants to meet you, David Van Patten 
and Tim Bryce at Harry's for drinks.

01:15:34.363 --> 01:15:35.656
Oh, God.

01:15:35.739 --> 01:15:37.783
What did you say, you dumb bitch?

01:15:38.367 --> 01:15:39.910
Patrick, I can't hear you.

01:15:39.993 --> 01:15:41.620
<i>What am I doing?</i>

01:15:42.287 --> 01:15:44.081
Where are you, Patrick? What's wrong?

01:15:45.832 --> 01:15:48.418
I don't think I'm gonna make it, Jean,

01:15:50.045 --> 01:15:52.381
to the office this afternoon.

01:15:52.881 --> 01:15:54.091
Why?

01:15:54.925 --> 01:15:57.010
<i>Just say no!</i>

01:15:58.262 --> 01:15:59.721
What is it, Patrick? Are you all right?

01:16:00.180 --> 01:16:03.475
Stop sounding so fucking sad!

01:16:04.476 --> 01:16:05.561
<i>Jesus!</i>

01:17:23.013 --> 01:17:24.473
Table for three.

01:17:24.556 --> 01:17:26.975
Bateman, you look a little wild-eyed. 
Rough day at the office?

01:17:27.851 --> 01:17:30.354
Hey, look, Bryce is back, 
and he's drinking mineral water.

01:17:30.437 --> 01:17:33.815
He's a changed man except he still can't 
get a reservation to save his life.

01:17:34.399 --> 01:17:36.068
Why don't you just try 150 Wooster?

01:17:36.693 --> 01:17:39.321
I'm not going anywhere 
unless we have a reservation.

01:17:39.655 --> 01:17:42.532
Le Cirque, Flamingo East, Oyster Bar.

01:17:42.616 --> 01:17:44.034
Come on, faggots, let's get a res.

01:17:44.117 --> 01:17:45.452
Keep your shirt on.

01:17:45.535 --> 01:17:46.953
Maybe lose the suspenders.

01:17:47.871 --> 01:17:49.539
Need a reservation for 8:30.

01:17:49.623 --> 01:17:50.874
Excuse me, gentlemen.

01:17:51.541 --> 01:17:52.709
Right back.

01:17:52.793 --> 01:17:54.586
10:00 would not be any good, no.

01:17:54.670 --> 01:17:56.004
Just fucking call them.

01:17:56.088 --> 01:17:58.006
- Give me the phone. I'll do it. 
- I'll call ya back.

01:17:58.090 --> 01:17:59.883
Face it. The Japanese will 
own most of this country

01:17:59.966 --> 01:18:02.803
<i>-by the end of the '90s. 
Shut up, Games.</i>

01:18:02.886 --> 01:18:04.221
They will not.

01:18:06.098 --> 01:18:07.683
So, Harold,

01:18:08.975 --> 01:18:09.226
did you get my message?

01:18:10.852 --> 01:18:12.813
Jesus, yes. That was hilarious.

01:18:12.896 --> 01:18:13.855
That was you, wasn't it?

01:18:13.939 --> 01:18:15.273
Yeah, naturally.

01:18:15.357 --> 01:18:17.150
Bateman killing Allen 
and the escort girls.

01:18:17.234 --> 01:18:18.777
That's fabulous. That's rich.

01:18:18.860 --> 01:18:20.028
What exactly do you mean?

01:18:20.112 --> 01:18:21.405
The message you left.

01:18:21.488 --> 01:18:23.156
By the way, Davis, how's Cynthia?

01:18:23.240 --> 01:18:24.449
You're still seeing her, right?

01:18:24.533 --> 01:18:26.368
Wait, Harold. What do you mean?

01:18:26.451 --> 01:18:28.078
Excuse me. Nothing.

01:18:28.161 --> 01:18:29.579
It's good to see you.

01:18:30.247 --> 01:18:31.540
Is that Edward Towers?

01:18:34.751 --> 01:18:36.002
Davis.

01:18:37.045 --> 01:18:39.005
I'm not one to badmouth anyone.

01:18:39.506 --> 01:18:40.507
Your joke was amusing,

01:18:40.590 --> 01:18:42.050
but come on, man.

01:18:42.134 --> 01:18:43.802
You had one fatal flaw.

01:18:45.011 --> 01:18:46.763
Bateman is such a dork.

01:18:47.472 --> 01:18:49.266
Such a boring, spineless lightweight.

01:18:50.475 --> 01:18:52.728
Now if you said Bryce or McDermott...

01:18:53.270 --> 01:18:54.688
Otherwise, it was amusing.

01:18:54.771 --> 01:18:56.815
Now if you'll excuse me, 
I really must be going.

01:18:56.898 --> 01:18:58.316
Wait.

01:18:59.651 --> 01:19:00.652
Stop.

01:19:02.112 --> 01:19:03.572
I did it, Carnes.

01:19:05.198 --> 01:19:06.450
I killed him.

01:19:06.533 --> 01:19:08.869
I'm Patrick Bateman.

01:19:12.414 --> 01:19:14.416
I chopped Allen's fucking head off.

01:19:15.834 --> 01:19:19.671
The whole message I left 
on your machine was true.

01:19:20.839 --> 01:19:22.090
Excuse me.

01:19:22.507 --> 01:19:23.842
I really must be going now.

01:19:24.593 --> 01:19:25.969
No, listen.

01:19:27.220 --> 01:19:28.889
Don't you know who I am?

01:19:29.556 --> 01:19:30.974
I'm not Davis.

01:19:31.057 --> 01:19:32.517
I'm Patrick Bateman.

01:19:35.353 --> 01:19:37.189
We talk on the phone all the time.

01:19:38.815 --> 01:19:40.400
Don't you recognize me?

01:19:42.486 --> 01:19:44.029
You're my lawyer.

01:19:45.906 --> 01:19:47.365
<i>Now, Games...</i>

01:19:48.408 --> 01:19:49.659
listen.

01:19:50.160 --> 01:19:51.786
Listen very, very carefully.

01:19:56.124 --> 01:19:57.918
I killed Paul Allen...

01:20:00.086 --> 01:20:01.546
and I liked it.

01:20:02.506 --> 01:20:04.591
I can't make myself any clearer.

01:20:05.592 --> 01:20:07.260
But that's simply not possible.

01:20:08.094 --> 01:20:09.513
And I don't find this funny anymore.

01:20:09.596 --> 01:20:11.640
It never was supposed to be.

01:20:12.057 --> 01:20:13.934
- Why isn't it possible? 
-lt's just not.

01:20:14.017 --> 01:20:16.728
Why not, you stupid bastard?

01:20:17.813 --> 01:20:20.649
Because I had dinner with 
Paul Allen twice in London,

01:20:21.858 --> 01:20:23.568
-just ten days ago. 
- No, you...

01:20:27.447 --> 01:20:28.532
didn't.

01:20:28.615 --> 01:20:30.116
Now, if you'll excuse me.

01:21:11.408 --> 01:21:13.785
<i>We've seen the results of that mistrust</i>

01:21:13.869 --> 01:21:16.580
<i>in the form of lies, divisions, 
and mistakes.</i>

01:21:17.122 --> 01:21:19.499
<i>We need to find a way to cooperate</i>

01:21:19.583 --> 01:21:21.668
<i>while realizing foreign policy</i>

01:21:21.751 --> 01:21:23.628
<i>can't be run by committee.</i>

01:21:24.421 --> 01:21:26.923
<i>And I believe there's now 
the growing sense</i>

01:21:27.007 --> 01:21:30.218
<i>that we can accomplish 
more by cooperating.</i>

01:21:31.136 --> 01:21:32.387
<i>And, in the end,</i>

01:21:32.470 --> 01:21:35.348
<i>this may be the eventual 
blessing in disguise</i>

01:21:35.432 --> 01:21:36.975
<i>to come out of the Iran-Contra mess.</i>

01:21:37.058 --> 01:21:38.810
How can he lie like that?

01:21:40.854 --> 01:21:42.731
- How can he pull that shit? 
- What shit?

01:21:42.814 --> 01:21:44.691
Now where do we have reservations at?

01:21:45.317 --> 01:21:47.986
I mean, I'm not really hungry, but 
I'd like to have reservations someplace.

01:21:48.069 --> 01:21:49.821
How can you be so fucking...

01:21:51.114 --> 01:21:52.407
I don't know...

01:21:52.490 --> 01:21:53.533
cool about it?

01:21:53.617 --> 01:21:55.702
Some guys are just born cool, I guess.

01:22:01.875 --> 01:22:03.209
Bateman.

01:22:04.294 --> 01:22:05.795
What are you so fucking zany about?

01:22:05.879 --> 01:22:08.173
I'm just a happy camper.

01:22:09.382 --> 01:22:10.634
Rockin' and a-rollin'!

01:22:12.677 --> 01:22:14.012
Oh, brother! Look,

01:22:14.095 --> 01:22:17.515
he presents himself 
as this harmless old codger, but

01:22:18.016 --> 01:22:19.100
inside...

01:22:19.184 --> 01:22:20.769
But inside...

01:22:21.978 --> 01:22:23.855
<i>But inside doesn't matter.</i>

01:22:25.106 --> 01:22:26.983
Inside? Yes? Inside?

01:22:27.067 --> 01:22:29.152
Believe it or not, Bryce, 
we're actually listening to you.

01:22:29.235 --> 01:22:30.820
Come on, Bateman,

01:22:30.904 --> 01:22:31.946
what do you think?

01:22:34.824 --> 01:22:36.117
Whatever.

01:22:36.201 --> 01:22:38.578
Whose moronic idea was it 
to order dry beers?

01:22:39.704 --> 01:22:41.206
I need a scotch.

01:22:57.347 --> 01:22:59.307
<i>There are no more barriers to cross.</i>

01:23:00.433 --> 01:23:04.062
<i>All I have in common 
with the uncontrollable and the insane,</i>

01:23:04.145 --> 01:23:06.106
<i>the vicious and the evil,</i>

01:23:06.189 --> 01:23:09.818
<i>all the mayhem I have caused 
and my utter indifference toward it,</i>

01:23:09.901 --> 01:23:11.778
<i>I have now surpassed.</i>

01:23:15.240 --> 01:23:17.534
<i>My pain is constant and sharp,</i>

01:23:18.034 --> 01:23:20.745
<i>and I do not hope 
for a better world for anyone.</i>

01:23:21.079 --> 01:23:25.542
<i>In fact, I want my pain 
to be inflicted on others.</i>

01:23:26.584 --> 01:23:28.420
<i>I want no one to escape.</i>

01:23:30.880 --> 01:23:32.882
<i>But even after admitting this,</i>

01:23:33.258 --> 01:23:34.884
<i>there is no catharsis.</i>

01:23:35.510 --> 01:23:37.929
<i>My punishment continues to elude me,</i>

01:23:38.346 --> 01:23:40.807
<i>and I gain no deeper knowledge of myself.</i>

01:23:41.641 --> 01:23:44.728
<i>No new knowledge can be 
extracted from my telling.</i>

01:23:45.478 --> 01:23:48.898
<i>This confession has meant nothing.</i>
